BJP <BJPaskoff@yahoo.com> wrote:
> How can I add sound to the Windows port of Nethack? The Guidebook 
> is really vague about this. I tried adding these lines to my 
> defaults.nh file: 
> 
 
> SOUNDDIR=D:/Games/Nethack/
> SOUND=MESG "hit" "Medium.wav" 100
> 
> Now it should play "Medium.wav" every time a message appears with 
> the word "hit" in it, but I don't hear anything. I have Silent 
> set to False if that does anything. 

Assuming that medium.wav really exists in D:\Games\Nethack,
your example would only play the sound if the entire message was 
"hit", so what you really want is something like:

SOUNDDIR=D:/Games/Nethack/
SOUND=MESG "* hit*" "Medium.wav" 100

Note however, that this would also play the sound for a
sentence containing a word such as " hither" (unlikely).

